{"id":634,"status":"Fixed","summary":"{function(number, string)} should not be assignable to {function(number)}","labels":["Type-Defect","Priority-Medium"],"stars":0,"commentCount":3,"comments":[{"id":0,"commenterId":4570684509025261907,"content":"Consider the following snippet. I don't think the &quot;second call&quot; should compile. As a side note: it would be great if none of the compiled in some pseudo-strict compile mode.

/** @param {function(string,number):boolean} param */
function func(param) {}

/** @type {function(string,number,boolean):boolean} */
function paramFunc1() {}

/** @type {function(string):boolean} */
function paramFunc2() {}

// first call
func(paramFunc1);

// second call
func(paramFunc2);
